  "dct_description_sm": [
    "The Photosynthetically Available Radiation (L2) layer displays photosynthetically available radiation over oceans and large bodies of water and is measured in einstein/m²/day.",
    "Photosynthetically Available Radiation (PAR) controls the growth of aquatic plants and, therefore, regulates the composition of marine ecosystems.",
    "A daily visualization from NASA's Global Imagery Browse Services (GIBS), available from 2000-02-24 and updated as new data arrive. Made from Terra MODIS Level-2 Regional Ocean Color (OC) Data, version 2022.0 (MODIST_L2_OC, version 2022.0, doi:10.5067/TERRA/MODIS/L2/OC/2022.0)."
